{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And Abraham was going… and YHWH said.</b> He was occupied with the commandment of acts of kindness to escort the guests, and YHWH said that He would reveal to him <b>so that he may command his children</b> — as they said of blessed memory (Avot 4:2): the reward of a commandment is a commandment." "<b>Shall I hide?</b> It is fitting not to hide from Abraham, in accordance with My attribute of goodness, and to make known to him that if among the wicked there were any quorum of righteous men through whom the wicked might yet have hope of repentance, I would incline toward mercy to spare even the wicked — perhaps they will repent, for He does not desire the death of the dead — and that when there is no hope of repentance, He will execute judgment upon them."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:36.702535137Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}